lesson: 259
title: Laying the party table
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: A table laid in full gives every person 5 things: a plate, a knife, a fork, a spoon and a glass.
explain: Count all the people (the family and the guests), multiply by 5, then take away what is already on the table.
explain: The 4 of us and 6 guests are 10 people: 10 × 5 = 50 things. If 12 are already laid, 50 − 12 = 38 more are needed.
vars: a=name b=name f=2..6 g=2..10 p=2..40
need: p < (f + g) * 5 - 1
answer: (f + g) * 5 - p
exercise: {a}'s family of {f} has {g} guests for dinner. {a} has already put {p} things on the table. How many more plates, knives, forks, spoons and glasses must {a.he} lay to finish the table?
exercise: The table is for {f} family members and {g} visitors. {p} plates, knives, forks, spoons and glasses are already out. How many more are needed so everyone has a full place?
exercise: {a} and {b} lay the party table for their {f} family members and {g} friends. They have laid {p} things so far. How many more do they still have to lay?
exercise: {f} people live in {a}'s house and {g} guests are coming. {a}'s brother has laid {p} of the things. How many plates, knives, forks, spoons and glasses are still to be put out?
exercise: For a dinner of {f} hosts and {g} guests, {p} items are on the table already. How many more items does a fully laid table need?
exercise: laying the table, {f} of us + {g} guests. {p} things out already. how many more plates knives forks spoons glasses
exercise: {f} of us, {g+1}, no wait {g} guests coming, {a} already put out {p} bits. how many more to finish laying it
exercise: we're {f}, {g} coming over, nan's bringing the pav, {p} things on the table so far. how many more for everyone to have the lot
exercise: {a} laid {p} things already for {f} fam n {g} guests. how many more till it's done
exercise: full table for {f} plus {g} guests, {p} things down. how many to go
test: The {g} guests and the {f} people of the house need full places. With {p} items already laid, how many more plates, knives, forks, spoons and glasses are wanted?
test: {b} has set out {p} pieces for a dinner of {f} hosts and {g} visitors. How many pieces must still be laid so that each place is complete?
test: How many items are left to lay if a table for {f} family and {g} guests already has {p} of its plates, knives, forks, spoons and glasses?
test: {f} fam {g} guests, {p} things laid. how many more
test: {a} says we're done already lol, {f} of us n {g} guests, {p} things down. nope. how many more really
test: tea for {f} of us n {g} visitors, {b} brought {g} candles, {p} things already on the table. how many more plates knives forks spoons glasses
exam: It is given that a table is to be laid in full for {f.words} members of a household and {g.words} guests, and that {p} items have hitherto been placed. Determine the number of plates, knives, forks, spoons and glasses yet to be laid.
exam: A dinner table is to be furnished with complete place settings for {f} residents and {g} visitors. Whereas {p} items are already in position, ascertain the quantity of items remaining to be laid.
exam: Compute the number of further plates, knives, forks, spoons and glasses necessitated by the complete laying of a table for {g} guests and {f} hosts, {p} items having been placed previously.
exam: In respect of a fully laid table for {f} family members and {g} invitees, of which {p} items are in place, state the number of items outstanding.
exercise: {a}'s family is {f} now that Grandad has passed away, and {g} guests come for dinner. {p} things are already on the table. How many more plates, knives, forks, spoons and glasses must {a} lay to finish the table?
exercise: dad's resting his eyes on the sofa, snoring, lazy sod, so {a} lays the table. {f} family, {g} guests, {p} things already out. how many more plates, knives, forks, spoons and glasses?
test: {b} helped, meaning {b.he} put out only {p} items and wandered off. The table needs a plate, knife, fork, spoon and glass for each of {f} family members and {g} visitors. How many items are still to be laid?
